D("reformism",{etymology:E("Formed from reform + -ism; reform comes from Latin reformare ‘form again’, and -ism names a political attitude or doctrine.","re-","formare","-ism","Etymonline, reform (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reformation); -ism (https://www.etymonline.com/word/-ism)."),contexts:[C("reformism.s1","政治思想","The party's reformism favors legal, gradual changes to labor law rather than a sudden overthrow of the institutions.","該政黨的改良主義偏好依法逐步修改勞工法，而非突然推翻制度。","Reformism is a political attitude seeking change through legal, step-by-step reform.","Reformism is the subject; favors takes gradual legal change as its object, while rather than contrasts alternatives.","The party seeks incremental change inside the existing legal framework.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The manifesto calls for immediate violent overthrow of every institution and labels that revolutionary rupture reformism.","The manifesto calls for immediate revolutionary rupture, not gradual legal reformism.","Reformism specifically seeks lawful, step-by-step change; overthrowing institutions at once is a different political approach.")],quiz:[Q("reformism.q1","reformism.s1","meaning","Reformism favors change that is generally ___.",["legal and gradual","violent and immediate","entirely impossible"],"legal and gradual","The source defines reformism as step-by-step legal reform.","meaning"),Q("reformism.q2","reformism.s1","context","Which platform best reflects reformism?",["Amend the law through lawful stages to improve worker protections","Abolish all institutions overnight by force","Keep all laws permanently unchanged"],"Amend the law through lawful stages to improve worker protections","It pursues incremental improvement within legal processes.","context"),Q("reformism.q3","reformism.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ism in reformism indicates a ___.",["doctrine or political attitude","person who officiates a match","place where oil is processed"],"doctrine or political attitude","-ism commonly names an ideology or approach.","word-formation"),Q("reformism.q4","reformism.s1","confusable","How does reformism differ from an abrupt revolution?",["It seeks step-by-step legal changes.","It always rejects any change.","It is a chemical process."],"It seeks step-by-step legal changes.","Gradual legal reform distinguishes reformism from sudden overthrow.","confusable")]});
D("refraction",{etymology:E("From Late Latin refractionem, from refringere ‘break or bend back’, re- ‘back’ + frangere ‘break’; English uses it for optical bending and an eye test of that bending.","re-","frangere","-tion","Etymonline, refraction (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refraction)."),contexts:[C("refraction.s1","物理","The glass prism separated white light into colors through refraction as the beam changed direction inside the material.","玻璃稜鏡中的光束改變方向，藉由折射將白光分解成不同顏色。","Refraction is the bending of light as it passes through water, glass, or another medium.","Through refraction names the process; as introduces the light's direction change.","Light changes direction when crossing into the prism and separates into colors."),C("refraction.s2","眼科","The optometrist performed a refraction to determine which lenses would focus the patient's vision clearly.","驗光師進行屈光檢查，以判定哪種鏡片能讓病人的視力清晰聚焦。","A refraction is a test of how well the eye bends light.","Performed a refraction is the procedure; to determine explains its purpose.","The eye test measures focusing so an appropriate lens prescription can be chosen.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The optometrist's refraction measured how sharply the patient heard quiet sounds through a prism.","The optometrist's refraction measured how the patient's eyes bent light to focus an image.","Refraction in optometry concerns the eye's bending of light, not hearing or sound intensity.")],quiz:[Q("refraction.q1","refraction.s1","meaning","Light refraction occurs when light ___.",["bends as it passes into another medium","is turned into a public vote","is absorbed by a referee"],"bends as it passes into another medium","Refraction is the bending of light through materials such as glass or water.","meaning"),Q("refraction.q2","refraction.s2","context","An eye-care professional performs a refraction to ___.",["test how the eye bends light and choose lenses","measure hearing range","purify sugar"],"test how the eye bends light and choose lenses","This is the optometry sense of refraction.","context"),Q("refraction.q3","refraction.s1","context","A straw looks shifted where it enters a glass of water because of ___.",["refraction","reformism","reimbursement"],"refraction","Light bends as it passes between water and air.","context"),Q("refraction.q4","refraction.s2","word-choice","The clinic scheduled a ____ before ordering the patient's glasses.",["refraction","refinery","reformer"],"refraction","The test determines how the eyes focus light for vision correction.","word-choice")]});
D("refractory",{etymology:E("From Latin refractarius ‘stubborn, resisting’, from refringere ‘break back’; the image is of resisting or breaking attempts to control, later extended to heat-resistant materials.","re-","frangere","-ory","Etymonline, refraction (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refraction)."),contexts:[C("refractory.s1","材料科學","The furnace lining used refractory brick that could withstand intense heat without melting.","爐壁內襯使用耐火磚，即使承受高熱也不會熔化。","Refractory can mean hard to melt, hard to cure, or stubbornly disobedient.","Refractory modifies brick; that-clause explains the material's heat resistance.","The brick remains solid under the furnace's high temperature.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The refractory alloy melted at room temperature and could not resist even a small increase in heat.","The refractory alloy resisted melting even when exposed to intense heat.","A refractory material is difficult to melt; the stated easy melting reverses the meaning.")],quiz:[Q("refractory.q1","refractory.s1","meaning","A refractory material is difficult to ___.",["melt","refer","refund"],"melt","The material sense refers to resistance to high heat.","meaning"),Q("refractory.q2","refractory.s1","context","Which item is refractory?",["A kiln brick that stays solid at very high temperatures","An ice cube that melts in a warm room","A paper note that dissolves in water"],"A kiln brick that stays solid at very high temperatures","Resistance to melting makes the brick refractory.","context"),Q("refractory.q3","refractory.s1","meaning","A refractory patient in a medical context may be one whose condition is ___.",["difficult to treat","easily cured at once","a direct public vote"],"difficult to treat","The source also includes hard to cure as a sense of refractory.","meaning"),Q("refractory.q4","refractory.s1","word-choice","The foundry chose ____ lining for its furnace walls.",["refractory","refreshing","refundable"],"refractory","The lining must resist extreme heat and melting.","word-choice")]});
D("refrain",{etymology:E("The verb came through Old French refraigner from Latin refrenare ‘bridle, restrain’ (re- + frenare); the repeated-song noun has a distinct history from Old French refrain and Latin refringere.","re-","frenare","verb and noun have distinct histories","Etymonline, refrain (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refrain)."),contexts:[C("refrain.s1","禮儀","Please refrain from using flash photography while the performers are on stage.","表演者在台上時，請避免使用閃光燈拍照。","To refrain from something is to stop yourself from doing it.","Refrain from is followed by the gerund using; while gives the time restriction.","The audience is asked to hold back from taking flash photos."),C("refrain.s2","音樂","The audience joined the singer for the refrain, repeating the same four lines at the end of each verse.","每段結尾時，觀眾都和歌手一起唱副歌，重複相同的四行歌詞。","A refrain is the repeated part of a song.","For the refrain identifies what the audience joined; repeating explains its structure.","The same lines recur after each verse."),C("refrain.s3","論述","“We need better evidence” became the director's refrain at every planning meeting.","「我們需要更好的證據」成了主管每次規劃會議都反覆提起的話。","A refrain can be a remark or idea that is repeated often.","Became the director's refrain assigns a recurring statement; at every meeting shows repetition.","The phrase is repeatedly said, not necessarily sung.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The notice asks visitors to refrain to touch the display cases.","The notice asks visitors to refrain from touching the display cases.","Refrain meaning avoid is followed by from + gerund, not a to-infinitive.")],quiz:[Q("refrain.q1","refrain.s1","grammar","Complete correctly: “Please refrain ___ eating in the gallery.”",["from","to","at"],"from","The verb takes the pattern refrain from + gerund.","grammar"),Q("refrain.q2","refrain.s2","meaning","The refrain of a song is the part that ___.",["is repeated","is used to cool food","is a public vote"],"is repeated","A song refrain recurs, often as a chorus.","meaning"),Q("refrain.q3","refrain.s3","context","A manager's refrain is “Check the source” at every meeting. It is ___.",["a remark repeated often","a one-time silent action","a heat-resistant brick"],"a remark repeated often","The source sense is a frequently repeated remark or idea.","context"),Q("refrain.q4","refrain.s1","word-choice","To avoid interrupting the speaker, the students had to ____ from calling out.",["refrain","refreeze","reform"],"refrain","Refrain from means stop oneself from an action.","word-choice")]});
D("refreeze",{etymology:E("A regular compound of re- ‘again’ + freeze, from Old English frēosan ‘turn to ice’; it means freeze something again or become frozen once more.","re-","frēosan","re- + freeze","Etymonline, refreeze (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refreeze); freeze (https://www.etymonline.com/word/freeze)."),contexts:[C("refreeze.s1","食品安全","Once the soup had thawed in the refrigerator, the cook reheated it instead of letting it refreeze on the counter.","湯在冰箱中解凍後，廚師選擇重新加熱，而不是讓它在檯面上再次結冰。","To refreeze is to turn into ice once more or store something frozen again.","Refreeze follows letting; instead of contrasts renewed freezing with reheating.","The word describes a second freezing after thawing.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","After the ice cream melted in the sun, they refroze it by leaving it beside the warm grill.","After the ice cream melted in the sun, they refroze it in a freezer.","To refreeze requires making it frozen again; a warm grill would not freeze melted ice cream.")],quiz:[Q("refreeze.q1","refreeze.s1","meaning","If water thaws and then refreezes, it ___.",["turns to ice again","stays liquid forever","becomes a reference"],"turns to ice again","The prefix re- indicates freezing once more.","meaning"),Q("refreeze.q2","refreeze.s1","context","A frozen meal has thawed but is still safe to store. To refreeze it, put it ___.",["back in a freezer","in direct sun","on a hot stove"],"back in a freezer","A freezer can turn it into ice again.","context"),Q("refreeze.q3","refreeze.s1","word-formation","What does re- add to freeze in refreeze?",["again","before","not"],"again","Refreeze means freeze again.","word-formation"),Q("refreeze.q4","refreeze.s1","word-choice","If a pond freezes, melts during a thaw, then freezes again, it will ___.",["refreeze","refrain","reflect"],"refreeze","The pond becomes frozen for a second time.","word-choice")]});
D("refresh",{etymology:E("From Old French refreschier, re- ‘again’ + a form of fresh; English adopted it for restoring strength, then extended it to updating displays and renewing memory.","re-","fresh","re- + fresh","Etymonline, refresh (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refresh)."),contexts:[C("refresh.s1","休息","A cool drink and ten minutes in the shade refreshed the hikers before the steep climb.","一杯涼飲料和十分鐘的樹蔭休息讓健行者恢復精神，能繼續爬陡坡。","To refresh someone is to make a tired person feel stronger or cooler.","Refreshed takes the hikers as its object; before gives the next activity.","The drink and rest restore their energy before exertion."),C("refresh.s2","資訊科技","Tap the icon to refresh the page and display the newest weather warning.","點選圖示以重新整理頁面，顯示最新的天氣警報。","To refresh a screen is to make it show the newest information.","Refresh is an infinitive after to; and links the action to its displayed result.","The command reloads the page's current data."),C("refresh.s3","學習","The tutor reviewed the old diagram to refresh the class's memory of how the circuit worked.","家教重新講解舊圖，喚起學生對電路運作方式的記憶。","To refresh someone's memory is to help them remember something.","Refresh takes memory as its object; of how identifies the remembered information.","Reviewing the diagram helps students recall familiar material.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","After a long shift, the cold shower refreshed him by making him feel even more exhausted and overheated.","After a long shift, the cold shower refreshed him by making him feel cooler and less tired.","Refresh in the restorative sense means improve energy or comfort, not make someone more exhausted.")],quiz:[Q("refresh.q1","refresh.s1","meaning","A short rest can refresh a tired runner by ___.",["restoring some energy","making the runner more exhausted","changing a referendum result"],"restoring some energy","Refresh means make a tired person feel stronger or cooler.","meaning"),Q("refresh.q2","refresh.s2","context","When a browser page is refreshed, it ___.",["loads or displays the newest information","turns a liquid into ice","writes a job reference"],"loads or displays the newest information","The screen sense means update its display.","context"),Q("refresh.q3","refresh.s3","collocation","A quick review can ____ your memory of the safety steps.",["refresh","refinery","reformism"],"refresh","Refresh one's memory means help someone recall information.","collocation"),Q("refresh.q4","refresh.s2","grammar","Choose the correct instruction for updating a page.",["Refresh the page to see the latest results.","Refresh to the page see latest results.","Refresh the page seeing yesterday's results only."],"Refresh the page to see the latest results.","The imperative verb takes page as its object; the infinitive states purpose.","grammar")]});
D("refreshed",{etymology:E("The past-participle adjective of refresh, from Old French refreschier (re- + fresh); it describes a person feeling better and less tired after rest or food.","re-","fresh","-ed","Etymonline, refresh (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refresh)."),contexts:[C("refreshed.s1","休息","After a quiet night and a proper breakfast, the crew felt refreshed enough to begin the long drive.","安靜睡了一晚並吃過早餐後，隊員們精神恢復，足以開始長途駕駛。","Refreshed means feeling better and less tired after rest or food.","Felt refreshed is a linking-verb construction; enough to introduces regained capacity.","Sleep and breakfast restore the crew's energy.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","After sleeping for two hours, Niko woke refreshed, feeling weaker, more tired, and unable to stand.","After sleeping for two hours, Niko woke exhausted, feeling weaker, more tired, and unable to stand.","Feeling more tired and weak is the opposite of feeling refreshed after rest.")],quiz:[Q("refreshed.q1","refreshed.s1","meaning","Someone who feels refreshed after a break feels ___.",["better and less tired","more exhausted than before","ready to vote in a referendum"],"better and less tired","Refreshed describes restored energy after rest or food.","meaning"),Q("refreshed.q2","refreshed.s1","context","Which person is likely to feel refreshed?",["A traveler after sleeping well and eating breakfast","A worker after staying awake all night","A runner after an injury worsens"],"A traveler after sleeping well and eating breakfast","Rest and food can restore energy.","context"),Q("refreshed.q3","refreshed.s1","word-form","In “They felt refreshed,” refreshed functions as a/an ___.",["adjective after a linking verb","plural noun","past-tense noun"],"adjective after a linking verb","It describes the subject's state after felt.","word form"),Q("refreshed.q4","refreshed.s1","word-choice","A weekend off left the nurse rested and ____ for Monday's shift.",["refreshed","refundable","refractory"],"refreshed","The break restored energy, so refreshed fits.","word-choice")]});
D("refresher",{etymology:E("From refresh + -er; the agent/instrument suffix forms a noun for something that refreshes knowledge or energy, including a review course or a cooling drink.","re-","fresh","-er","Etymonline, refresh (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refresh)."),contexts:[C("refresher.s1","培訓","Before using the new equipment, staff attended a refresher on emergency shutdown procedures.","使用新設備前，員工參加了緊急關機程序的複習課。","A refresher is something that brings knowledge or energy back, such as a short review course.","Attended a refresher is followed by on to identify the course topic.","The class reviews procedures staff already learned, renewing their knowledge.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The annual refresher introduced an unrelated subject for the first time and did not review any previous training.","The annual refresher reviewed familiar safety procedures so staff could recall them.","A refresher renews existing knowledge or energy; first-time unrelated instruction is not a review refresher.")],quiz:[Q("refresher.q1","refresher.s1","meaning","A refresher course is designed to ___.",["review knowledge someone learned earlier","teach an unrelated subject with no review","replace a refrigerator"],"review knowledge someone learned earlier","A refresher brings knowledge back by reviewing it.","meaning"),Q("refresher.q2","refresher.s1","context","A driver takes a refresher after years away from the road to ___.",["review safe driving skills","vote in a public referendum","refine crude oil"],"review safe driving skills","The course renews knowledge and confidence.","context"),Q("refresher.q3","refresher.s1","word-formation","The noun refresher is related to the verb ___.",["refresh","refer","refute"],"refresh","A refresher is something that refreshes knowledge or energy.","word-formation"),Q("refresher.q4","refresher.s1","meaning","Which can be called a refresher under this entry?",["a short course reviewing emergency procedures","a new fuel tank","a device that bends light"],"a short course reviewing emergency procedures","A review course restores prior knowledge.","meaning")]});
D("refreshing",{etymology:E("Present-participle adjective from refresh, formed from Old French refreschier (re- + fresh); it came to describe something invigorating and later a welcome new or different approach.","re-","fresh","-ing","Etymonline, refresh (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refresh)."),contexts:[C("refreshing.s1","天氣","A refreshing breeze cooled the runners as they finished the shaded part of the trail.","一陣清爽的微風吹來，讓跑者在完成有樹蔭的路段時涼快不少。","Refreshing can mean cool and pleasant in a way that gives energy.","Refreshing modifies breeze; as introduces the time and effect.","The cool breeze makes the tired runners feel more comfortable."),C("refreshing.s2","溝通","It was refreshing to hear the candidate admit what she did not know and explain how she would find out.","聽到候選人坦承自己不知道的事，並說明會如何查證，令人耳目一新。","Refreshing can describe something new and different in a welcome way.","It was refreshing to hear is an evaluative construction; and links the welcome behaviors.","The unusual honesty is pleasantly different from evasive answers.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The refreshing air was hot, stale, and left everyone feeling more tired than before.","The stifling air was hot and stale, leaving everyone more tired than before.","Refreshing describes cool pleasant conditions that restore energy; the described air is oppressive.")],quiz:[Q("refreshing.q1","refreshing.s1","meaning","A refreshing breeze is ___.",["cool and pleasant, giving a sense of energy","hot and airless","a device that returns light"],"cool and pleasant, giving a sense of energy","That is the invigorating physical sense.","meaning"),Q("refreshing.q2","refreshing.s2","context","Why might an honest answer be refreshing?",["It is welcome and pleasantly different from evasive replies.","It is physically cold.","It is a chemical refrigerant."],"It is welcome and pleasantly different from evasive replies.","Refreshing can mean new and different in a welcome way.","context"),Q("refreshing.q3","refreshing.s1","collocation","After the hot walk, the swimmers enjoyed a ____ drink of water.",["refreshing","refractory","refundable"],"refreshing","The water cools and revives them.","collocation"),Q("refreshing.q4","refreshing.s2","meaning","A refreshing change is one that feels ___.",["pleasantly new","exactly the same and unwelcome","impossible to reach"],"pleasantly new","This sense is something new and different in a welcome way.","meaning")]});
D("refreshment",{etymology:E("From Old French refreschement, from refreschier ‘refresh, renew’ (re- + fresh); the noun first named restoration or aid and later food and drinks served to guests.","re-","fresh","-ment","Etymonline, refresh (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refresh)."),contexts:[C("refreshment.s1","活動","The conference volunteers placed water, fruit, and other refreshments on a table outside the lecture hall.","研討會志工將水、水果與其他茶點放在演講廳外的桌上。","Refreshments are food and drinks served to guests.","Refreshments is the object of placed; outside locates the table.","The plural refers to snacks and beverages available to attendees."),C("refreshment.s2","休息","A short walk in the garden gave the hikers a welcome sense of refreshment after the long climb.","長途攀登後，在花園短暫散步讓健行者重新感到精神爽快。","Refreshment can also mean the state of feeling fresh or energetic again.","Gave them a sense of refreshment takes a feeling as its object; after gives the preceding exertion.","The walk restores their energy after climbing.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The refreshments was served in the lobby before the talk.","The refreshments were served in the lobby before the talk.","Refreshments is plural in this food-and-drink sense, so it takes the plural verb were.")],quiz:[Q("refreshment.q1","refreshment.s1","meaning","At a meeting, refreshments are ___.",["food and drinks offered to guests","a legal vote","a kind of heat-resistant brick"],"food and drinks offered to guests","This is the catering sense of refreshments.","meaning"),Q("refreshment.q2","refreshment.s2","context","After a rest, the climbers felt a sense of refreshment. They felt ___.",["fresh and energetic again","more tired than ever","ready to refine sugar"],"fresh and energetic again","The second sense is renewed energy or freshness.","context"),Q("refreshment.q3","refreshment.s1","plural","Choose the natural sentence for several snacks and drinks.",["Refreshments are available in the lobby.","A refreshments is available in the lobby.","Refreshments is available in the lobby."],"Refreshments are available in the lobby.","The catering sense is commonly plural and takes a plural verb.","plural"),Q("refreshment.q4","refreshment.s1","collocation","The invitation says light ____ will be served after the talk.",["refreshments","refractories","referents"],"refreshments","Light refreshments is a standard phrase for small snacks and drinks.","collocation")]});
D("refrigerant",{etymology:E("From refrigerate/refrigeration and the Latin present participle ending -ant; Latin refrigerare means ‘make cool’, from re- + frigerare, based on frigus ‘cold’.","re-","frigus","-ant","Etymonline, refrigerate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refrigerate)."),contexts:[C("refrigerant.s1","暖通空調","The technician recovered the refrigerant from the air conditioner before opening the sealed cooling circuit.","技術員在打開密封冷卻迴路前，先回收空調中的冷媒。","A refrigerant is a fluid that evaporates and condenses inside a cooling machine.","Recovered the refrigerant takes the fluid as its object; before marks the safety sequence.","The fluid circulates through the sealed system and changes state to move heat.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The technician poured refrigerant into the kitchen as if it were a bottled drink for cooling guests.","The technician charged the cooling system with refrigerant, a working fluid that circulates inside the machine.","Refrigerant is a fluid used in a cooling system, not a beverage for people to drink.")],quiz:[Q("refrigerant.q1","refrigerant.s1","meaning","A refrigerant is the fluid that ___.",["circulates and changes state inside cooling equipment","is served as a cold drink","is used as a ballot"],"circulates and changes state inside cooling equipment","It evaporates and condenses to help a machine remove heat.","meaning"),Q("refrigerant.q2","refrigerant.s1","context","Which situation involves refrigerant?",["A technician checks the sealed fluid loop in an air conditioner.","A referee checks the score.","A librarian checks a book citation."],"A technician checks the sealed fluid loop in an air conditioner.","Cooling equipment uses refrigerant in a circulating loop.","context"),Q("refrigerant.q3","refrigerant.s1","confusable","Refrigerant is different from a refrigerator because refrigerant is ___.",["the working fluid; a refrigerator is the cooling appliance","the appliance; a refrigerator is the fluid","the food kept inside the appliance"],"the working fluid; a refrigerator is the cooling appliance","The suffix and source senses distinguish the fluid from the machine.","confusable"),Q("refrigerant.q4","refrigerant.s1","word-choice","A leak detector was used to locate escaping ____ in the cooling unit.",["refrigerant","refreshment","referee"],"refrigerant","The cooling unit's working fluid is refrigerant.","word-choice")]});
D("refrigerate",{etymology:E("From Latin refrigeratus, past participle of refrigerare ‘make cool or cold’; the verb was back-formed from refrigeration or borrowed from the Latin form.","re-","frigus","-ate","Etymonline, refrigerate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refrigerate)."),contexts:[C("refrigerate.s1","食品保存","Refrigerate the cooked rice within two hours and keep it covered until it is reheated.","熟飯應在兩小時內冷藏，並加蓋保存直到重新加熱。","To refrigerate is to keep something at a low temperature, usually in a refrigerator.","Refrigerate is an imperative; within two hours sets the deadline and until marks the storage period.","Cold storage slows spoilage before the rice is reheated.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","To keep the milk safely cold overnight, refrigerate it on the sunny counter beside the oven.","To keep the milk safely cold overnight, refrigerate it in the refrigerator.","A sunny counter beside an oven is not a low-temperature place; refrigerating means keeping something cold.")],quiz:[Q("refrigerate.q1","refrigerate.s1","meaning","To refrigerate leftovers is to ___.",["keep them at a low temperature","heat them until boiling","leave them in direct sunlight"],"keep them at a low temperature","Refrigerating means cold storage, usually in a refrigerator.","meaning"),Q("refrigerate.q2","refrigerate.s1","context","Where should a cook refrigerate fresh milk?",["In the refrigerator","On a warm windowsill","Beside a hot oven"],"In the refrigerator","The appliance keeps food and drink at a low temperature.","context"),Q("refrigerate.q3","refrigerate.s1","grammar","Choose the correct instruction.",["Refrigerate the sauce after it cools.","Refrigerate to the sauce after it cools.","Refrigerate the sauce to coldly."],"Refrigerate the sauce after it cools.","Refrigerate is a transitive verb and directly takes sauce as its object.","grammar"),Q("refrigerate.q4","refrigerate.s1","word-choice","The label says to ____ the medicine after opening.",["refrigerate","reformism","reflect"],"refrigerate","The instruction means keep the medicine cold.","word-choice")]});
D("refrigeration",{etymology:E("From Latin refrigerationem, the noun of action from refrigerare ‘cool down’; re- + frigerare is based on frigus ‘cold’.","re-","frigus","-ation","Etymonline, refrigerate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refrigerate)."),contexts:[C("refrigeration.s1","食品工業","Reliable refrigeration kept the vaccine shipment within its required temperature range throughout transport.","可靠的冷藏設備在運送全程使疫苗保持於規定溫度範圍內。","Refrigeration is the use of machines to remove heat and keep goods at a low temperature.","Refrigeration is the subject; kept takes the shipment as its object, and throughout sets duration.","The cooling system removes heat and preserves temperature-sensitive goods.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The warehouse used refrigeration to raise the room temperature and keep frozen food warm.","The warehouse used refrigeration to remove heat and keep frozen food cold.","Refrigeration removes heat to maintain low temperatures; warming food is the opposite purpose.")],quiz:[Q("refrigeration.q1","refrigeration.s1","meaning","Refrigeration is a process that ___.",["removes heat to keep goods cold","adds heat to cook goods","organizes a public vote"],"removes heat to keep goods cold","This is the machinery-based cooling sense.","meaning"),Q("refrigeration.q2","refrigeration.s1","context","A refrigerated truck uses refrigeration to ___.",["keep temperature-sensitive cargo cold during delivery","turn its cargo into fuel","make its cargo easier to read"],"keep temperature-sensitive cargo cold during delivery","The cooling system maintains a low temperature during transport.","context"),Q("refrigeration.q3","refrigeration.s1","word-formation","Refrigeration is the noun for the process related to ___.",["refrigerate","referee","reform"],"refrigerate","The noun names the act or system of cooling by refrigerating.","word-formation"),Q("refrigeration.q4","refrigeration.s1","collocation","The laboratory installed ____ to protect its heat-sensitive samples.",["refrigeration","reformation","refraction"],"refrigeration","The samples need low-temperature storage.","collocation")]});
D("refrigerator",{etymology:E("From refrigerate + -or, the instrument suffix; the appliance name follows the verb derived from Latin refrigerare ‘make cool’.","re-","frigus","-or","Etymonline, refrigerate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refrigerate)."),contexts:[C("refrigerator.s1","家電","She put the milk in the refrigerator so it would stay cold through the weekend.","她把牛奶放進冰箱，讓它整個週末都保持低溫。","A refrigerator is a large kitchen machine that keeps food and drink cold.","Put the milk in the refrigerator states placement and purpose; so introduces the intended result.","The household appliance maintains the milk at a low temperature."),C("refrigerator.s2","醫療保存","The clinic stored temperature-sensitive specimens in a locked refrigerator cabinet set to four degrees.","診所將對溫度敏感的樣本存放在設定為四度的上鎖冷藏櫃中。","A refrigerator can also be any cabinet or room used to keep things at a low temperature.","Refrigerator cabinet is the object of stored; set to gives the cabinet's temperature.","The term refers to a cold-storage cabinet outside the ordinary kitchen-appliance use.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The nurse stored the vaccine in a refrigerator heated to 35 degrees so it would remain safely chilled.","The nurse stored the vaccine in a refrigerator kept at the required low temperature.","A refrigerator keeps items cold; a warm setting would not preserve a temperature-sensitive vaccine safely.")],quiz:[Q("refrigerator.q1","refrigerator.s1","meaning","A household refrigerator is a machine that ___.",["keeps food and drinks cold","makes fuel from crude oil","bends light through glass"],"keeps food and drinks cold","This is the common kitchen-appliance sense.","meaning"),Q("refrigerator.q2","refrigerator.s2","context","A laboratory refrigerator cabinet is used to ___.",["store samples at low temperature","heat specimens for cooking","hold books for reference"],"store samples at low temperature","The broader sense includes cabinets or rooms for cold storage.","context"),Q("refrigerator.q3","refrigerator.s1","confusable","How does refrigerator differ from refrigerant?",["The refrigerator is the machine; refrigerant is the working fluid inside a cooling system.","A refrigerator is a liquid; refrigerant is a kitchen appliance.","They both mean an ice cube."],"The refrigerator is the machine; refrigerant is the working fluid inside a cooling system.","The appliance contains or uses the refrigerant to move heat.","confusable"),Q("refrigerator.q4","refrigerator.s1","collocation","Put the leftover soup in the ____ before it spoils.",["refrigerator","refraction","reformism"],"refrigerator","The appliance keeps food cold.","word-choice")]});
D("refuel",{etymology:E("Formed in 1811 from re- ‘again’ + fuel; it first had a figurative sense and later came to mean supplying a vehicle or machine with fuel again.","re-","fuel","re- + fuel","Etymonline, refuel (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refuel)."),contexts:[C("refuel.s1","交通","The pilot landed at the island airport to refuel the aircraft before the longer flight north.","飛行員在島上機場降落，為飛機加油後再向北進行較長航程。","To refuel is to put more fuel into a vehicle or machine.","Refuel takes the aircraft as its object; before introduces the planned next leg.","The aircraft receives additional fuel so it can continue flying.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The mechanic refueled the electric bicycle by pouring gasoline into its battery compartment.","The mechanic recharged the electric bicycle's battery.","An electric bicycle's battery is charged electrically; refuel means add fuel to an engine or machine that uses fuel.")],quiz:[Q("refuel.q1","refuel.s1","meaning","To refuel a car is to ___.",["put more fuel into it","remove all its fuel","cool it in a refrigerator"],"put more fuel into it","The verb means supply a vehicle or machine with fuel again.","meaning"),Q("refuel.q2","refuel.s1","context","A pilot stops at an airport to refuel before a long flight. The crew ___.",["adds fuel to the aircraft","reads out passenger names","reforms the runway"],"adds fuel to the aircraft","Refueling lets the aircraft continue its journey.","context"),Q("refuel.q3","refuel.s1","word-formation","In refuel, re- means ___.",["again","without","under"],"again","The tank is supplied with fuel again.","word-formation"),Q("refuel.q4","refuel.s1","confusable","For an electric bicycle, the usual action is to ____ the battery, not refuel it with gasoline.",["recharge","refrigerate","referee"],"recharge","A battery is charged with electricity; it is not a gasoline fuel tank.","confusable")]});
D("refuge",{etymology:E("From Old French refuge and Latin refugium ‘a place to flee back to’, from re- ‘back’ + fugere ‘flee’; it names both protection and a place providing safety.","re-","fugere","-ium","Etymonline, refugee (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refugee)."),contexts:[C("refuge.s1","安全","The residents sought refuge from the wildfire in a school gym outside the evacuation zone.","居民在疏散區外的學校體育館尋求野火庇護。","Refuge is protection from danger or trouble.","Sought refuge from names the danger; in introduces where protection was found.","The residents find safety from the fire in a protected area."),C("refuge.s2","野生動物","The wetland refuge gives migrating birds a protected place to rest and feed.","這處濕地保護區為候鳥提供安全的休息與覓食場所。","A refuge can be a place that protects people or animals.","Refuge is modified by wetland; gives takes place as its object.","The protected wetland shelters migrating birds.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The hikers found refuge in the exposed ravine during the storm, where there was no shelter from wind or falling rocks.","The hikers found refuge in a sheltered cave during the storm, away from wind and falling rocks.","A refuge provides protection; the exposed ravine described offers no safety from the stated danger.")],quiz:[Q("refuge.q1","refuge.s1","meaning","To seek refuge from a storm is to seek ___.",["protection from danger","a source citation","a warmer engine"],"protection from danger","Refuge can mean safety or protection from trouble.","meaning"),Q("refuge.q2","refuge.s2","context","Which could be a wildlife refuge?",["A protected marsh where birds can rest","A factory that purifies sugar","A book of grammar rules"],"A protected marsh where birds can rest","The place protects animals and gives them habitat.","context"),Q("refuge.q3","refuge.s1","collocation","The family sought ____ from the flood in a community shelter.",["refuge","reflectance","referee"],"refuge","Seek refuge from danger is a common collocation.","collocation"),Q("refuge.q4","refuge.s2","meaning","A refuge for injured animals is ___.",["a place that shelters and protects them","a person who recommends an employee","an instrument for shaving"],"a place that shelters and protects them","The place sense is somewhere that protects people or animals.","meaning")]});
D("refugee",{etymology:E("Borrowed from French refugié, a noun use of the past participle of refugier ‘take shelter’; it derives from Latin refugium, re- ‘back’ + fugere ‘flee’.","re-","fugere","-ee","Etymonline, refugee (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refugee)."),contexts:[C("refugee.s1","人道援助","The family became refugees after fighting forced them to leave their country and seek safety across the border.","戰火迫使這家人離開祖國並越境尋求安全，他們因此成為難民。","A refugee is someone forced to leave their country because of war or danger.","Became refugees is followed by after-clause explaining the cause; and coordinates leaving and seeking safety.","Conflict forces the family to cross a border for protection.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The tourists who chose to move abroad for a holiday were refugees because they crossed an international border.","The tourists who chose to move abroad for a holiday were travelers; refugees are forced to flee danger.","Crossing a border voluntarily for a holiday does not make someone a refugee; the source sense requires forced flight from war or danger.")],quiz:[Q("refugee.q1","refugee.s1","meaning","A refugee is forced to leave home because of ___.",["war or danger","a planned vacation","a library assignment"],"war or danger","The source definition centers forced departure because of danger.","meaning"),Q("refugee.q2","refugee.s1","context","Which person is a refugee?",["Someone who flees across a border to escape armed conflict","Someone who takes a chosen weekend trip","Someone who changes jobs in the same town"],"Someone who flees across a border to escape armed conflict","The person has been forced to leave because of danger.","context"),Q("refugee.q3","refugee.s1","confusable","Why is a refugee different from an ordinary tourist?",["A refugee is forced to flee danger; a tourist travels by choice.","A refugee is always a travel guide.","A tourist is a protected wildlife area."],"A refugee is forced to flee danger; a tourist travels by choice.","The distinction is whether flight from danger compelled the move.","confusable"),Q("refugee.q4","refugee.s1","word-choice","The aid center provided blankets to each newly arrived ____ fleeing the conflict.",["refugee","reformer","refinery"],"refugee","The person has fled danger and needs shelter.","word-choice")]});
D("refund",{etymology:E("From Old French refunder and Latin refundere ‘give back, restore, literally pour back’, re- ‘back’ + fundere ‘pour’; the money sense developed from repayment.","re-","fundere","re- + fund","Etymonline, refund (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refund)."),contexts:[C("refund.s1","消費","The shop issued a full refund after the headphones stopped working during the return period.","耳機在退貨期限內故障後，商店退還了全額款項。","A refund is money paid back to a customer.","Issued a refund is a verb-noun construction; after gives the reason for repayment.","The customer receives the purchase money back."),C("refund.s2","消費","If the event is cancelled, the organizer will refund every ticket buyer within five business days.","若活動取消，主辦單位將在五個工作天內退還每位購票者的款項。","To refund is to pay money back to the person who paid it.","Refund is a transitive verb with ticket buyer as object; if states the condition.","The buyers receive their payments back after cancellation.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The store refund the customer yesterday after the defective kettle was returned.","The store refunded the customer yesterday after the defective kettle was returned.","The past-time marker yesterday requires the past-tense verb refunded.")],quiz:[Q("refund.q1","refund.s1","meaning","A refund is ___.",["money returned to a customer","a charge added to a bill","a book used for lookup"],"money returned to a customer","The noun means a repayment of money previously paid.","meaning"),Q("refund.q2","refund.s2","context","The shop will refund the buyer if the item arrives broken. The shop will ___.",["pay the buyer's money back","ask the buyer to vote","refine the broken item into fuel"],"pay the buyer's money back","This is the verb meaning return money to the payer.","context"),Q("refund.q3","refund.s2","grammar","Choose the correct past-tense sentence.",["The store refunded me yesterday.","The store refund me yesterday.","The store refunding me yesterday."],"The store refunded me yesterday.","A completed action in the past takes refunded.","grammar"),Q("refund.q4","refund.s1","collocation","Keep your receipt if you need to request a ____.",["refund","reformism","refrigerant"],"refund","Request a refund is the usual customer-service phrase.","collocation")]});
D("refundable",{etymology:E("Formed from refund + -able, from French -able and Latin -abilis ‘capable of being’; the adjective describes a payment that can be returned under stated conditions.",null,"refund","-able","Etymonline, refund (https://www.etymonline.com/word/refund); -able (https://www.etymonline.com/word/-able)."),contexts:[C("refundable.s1","旅遊","The hotel offered a refundable deposit if guests cancelled before the stated deadline.","飯店表示，若房客在規定期限前取消，押金可以退還。","Refundable describes a payment the payer can get back under stated conditions.","Refundable modifies deposit; if-clause states the condition for repayment.","The deposit is returned only when cancellation meets the deadline condition.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The airline advertised a refundable ticket but refused to return the fare under any circumstance, including its own cancellation.","The airline advertised a nonrefundable ticket if it would not return the fare under any circumstance.","Refundable means the payer can get the payment back under stated conditions; refusing all repayment contradicts that promise.")],quiz:[Q("refundable.q1","refundable.s1","meaning","A refundable payment is one that ___.",["can be returned under stated conditions","must never be paid back","is made from cold fluid"],"can be returned under stated conditions","The adjective means the payer may get the money back if conditions are met.","meaning"),Q("refundable.q2","refundable.s1","context","A hotel deposit is refundable if cancelled by Friday. What happens when a guest cancels Thursday?",["The deposit can be returned under the stated rule.","The deposit becomes a referee.","The deposit is frozen into ice."],"The deposit can be returned under the stated rule.","Thursday meets the stated before-Friday condition.","context"),Q("refundable.q3","refundable.s1","word-formation","In refundable, -able means ___.",["capable of being refunded","one who refunds","a process of cooling"],"capable of being refunded","The suffix forms an adjective meaning able to be returned.","word-formation"),Q("refundable.q4","refundable.s1","confusable","A nonrefundable fare differs from a refundable fare because the nonrefundable fare ___.",["cannot be returned under the stated policy","is always returned automatically","is a type of cooling fluid"],"cannot be returned under the stated policy","The prefix non- negates the possibility of refund.","confusable")]});
